    "narrative": "The Austin Waves' offensive core is anchored today by **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, whose 69.27 efficiency score makes him our premier start. Facing MacKenzie Gore, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** benefits from a favorable park factor and a substantial platoon advantage against the southpaw, which helps mitigate the volatility of an unconfirmed lineup. While the rest of our active infield faces stiffer resistance\u2014particularly **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Jacob Wilson**, and **Josh Jung**\u2014each player retains a positive enough outlook to avoid the bench. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** is the most concerning play among the starters; his score of 41.68 is suppressed significantly by an 19% penalty against the elite arm of Cristopher S\u00e1nchez and a negative platoon split, but his premium spot in the order keeps him just above our \"Below floor\" threshold.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Nasim Nunez**, who finished with a 39.04 efficiency rating. While **Nasim Nunez** offers the elite sprint speed we prioritize for stolen base upside, the optimizer penalized his value due to the unfavorable matchup against S\u00e1nchez and a projected #9 spot in the lineup, which limits his counting stat potential. He fell just short of displacing **Jacob Wilson** or **Josh Jung** in a day where we must balance our aggressive need for speed against the reality of facing a difficult opposing starter. \n\nRisk management remains a primary focus, as the lineup pending status for our entire starting infield introduces a high degree of situational variance. We are monitoring the weather and confirmed lineups closely, as any shuffle down the order for **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** or his counterparts would necessitate a shift in our daily projections. With **Luis Robert Jr.** remaining sidelined on the IL and **Jackson Merrill** caught in a scheduling void, we are leaning on the current four-man infield to carry the weight while preserving our remaining game 